jobs.prompt:
Use case: ui-mockup.
Asset type: one high-fidelity portrait mobile GAME screenshot for a review of an existing Unity game's complete UI redesign, selected B / 2D Toon Bold.
Output: ONE full bleed 9:16 portrait screenshot, ideally 1080x1920. No phone frame, mockup on a desk, contact sheet, split panel, annotation, or browser chrome.
Reference images are VISUAL STYLE REFERENCES for a new screen, not pixel-locked edit targets. Preserve the selected design's identity: vivid sky blue #2EB9EF, a few low-contrast simple cloud silhouettes at edges, sunny cream #FFF6D8 surfaces, very heavy clean ink-navy #071B52 outlines, broad rounded playful lettering, round-cornered square tiles, large thumb-friendly buttons and crisp single flat offset shadows. Rich clean flat 2D cartoon artwork. Coral red #FF3E43, cobalt blue #0068FF, violet #8A25F5 are gameplay colors. Solid fills, minimal shading. The board stays front-facing and flat, never isometric. Do not reinvent the style or add a mascot.
Game name remains COLOR TRACE for this review because a replacement name has not been approved.
Constraints: no currency, lives, timers, stars, ratings, hint, shop, level selection map, settings, leaderboard, ads, watermarks or invented game mechanics. Every screen has ample edge safety, no clipped text, no tiny text. English UI. Keep all gameplay tiles countable.
Primary request: INCORRECT ANSWER feedback state for Stage3. Input1 is the gameplay LAYOUT reference; preserve its exact full size board, header, home, mixing legend, reset tray and all positions. Input2 is only a SOLVED BOARD FILL/ROUTE reference; do NOT inherit Input2's shrunk board, confetti, result layout or next-stage button. Stage layout: small square blue HOME icon button at top right, centered large cream pill with navy outlined title "STAGE 3", smaller "TRACE & MIX" below. Main board centered, taking about 90 percent of screen width, exactly FIVE columns and FOUR rows (20 equal square tiles), thick rounded navy outer frame, cream inset, white tile interiors, navy neutral tile borders, even gaps. Rows counted TOP TO BOTTOM, columns LEFT TO RIGHT. Red start solid circle at row1 col5 and blue start at row4 col1. Red target SQUARE tile outline r1c3, blue target SQUARE tile outline r4c3, separate purple SQUARE outlines r2c3 and r3c3 with a visible gap; not circular markers and not a merged two-cell outline. Below board: compact cream outlined mixing capsule, red circle + blue circle = purple circle. Bottom cream tray labelled "RESET", exactly three large reset buttons: left neutral charcoal with white circular arrow and "ALL", middle cobalt blue circular arrow, right coral red circular arrow. Board around y=430..1210 in a 1080x1920 conceptual canvas; keep header, capsule and bottom tray well separated. Same layout and dimensions across all gameplay states.
Draw the following near-completed board on the full-size gameplay grid:
row1 BLUE BLUE RED RED RED;
row2 BLUE BLUE RED RED RED;
row3 BLUE BLUE PURPLE RED RED;
row4 BLUE BLUE BLUE RED RED.
The actual completed Stage3 board is 5 columns x 4 rows. Fill every tile:
row1 BLUE BLUE RED RED RED;
row2 BLUE BLUE PURPLE RED RED;
row3 BLUE BLUE PURPLE RED RED;
row4 BLUE BLUE BLUE RED RED.
Show darker color routes over lighter matching tile face fills, so lines remain visible. Red origin r1c5 route down column5 to r4c5, left to r4c4, up column4 to r1c4, left to r1c3, down to r3c3. Blue origin r4c1 route up column1 to r1c1, right to r1c2, down column2 to r4c2, right to r4c3, up column3 to r2c3. Overlap is PURPLE along r2c3-r3c3. Only origin circles at r1c5 and r4c1, no endpoint dots everywhere. Red, blue and both purple target square borders remain visible.
IMPORTANT the above solved description is modified for this ONE INCORRECT CASE: the blue route STOPS at r3c3, so r2c3 has ONLY RED face and a red line, while r3c3 remains PURPLE. r2c3 is the ONLY incorrect tile: its target frame still specifies PURPLE. Preserve all other cells, origins and routes. Represent a snapshot in the 2-second opacity blink: r2c3's red tile face AND its purple square target perimeter are visibly faded to about 40% opacity; neighboring tiles remain fully vivid. Do not replace this cell with a red exclamation/cross or invent a danger tile. The line stays intact and every drawn path remains. No modal, no banner, no TRY AGAIN button, no shake lines, no confetti, no new feedback text. Only the existing Stage3 header, tagline, RESET and ALL labels. The two reset color buttons remain available to correct the paths.
